.TH ag-remote-events 1  "events 0.3.0-beta.7"
.SH NAME
ag\-remote\-events \- Show the events of the repository (replay), or follow them live
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag remote events\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-repository\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-cursor\fR] [\fB\-\-checkpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-from\-start\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-after\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-topics\fR] [\fB\-\-follow\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the events of the repository (replay), or follow them live
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR
Remote to use (default: origin)
.TP
\fB\-\-repository\fR \fI<OWNER/NAME>\fR
Explicit repository on the same server; repeat for up to 30 repositories
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fI<CURSOR>\fR
Resume the opaque cursor returned by the previous page
.TP
\fB\-\-checkpoint\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Load a saved cursor, then atomically replace it after emitted events
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-start\fR
Deliberately include history; otherwise a new feed starts from now
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Maximum events in the replay page (default: 100; maximum: 1000)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-\-after\fR \fI<AFTER>\fR [default: 0]
Replay events after this sequence number
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-\-topics\fR \fI<TOPICS>\fR
Only these topics (prefix match), e.g. `stream,proposal`
.TP
\fB\-\-follow\fR
Keep following new events
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0\-beta.7
